nother girl waiting somewhere in the background. I don't want a second option. I don't want someone else to replace you the moment things become complicated. I already have you, and I don't want anybody else. As long as nasa akin ka, pahahalagahan kita. I will continue choosing you, respecting you, and protecting what we have. And if you ever forget where I stand, come back to this. Read it again and remember that there is someone here who isn't secretly looking for someone better, prettier, or different. I already know who I want. I believe loyalty is a two-way street. If you give me yours, expect mine in return. But more than that, I want you to know that I'm loyal to you because I genuinely want to be, not because I'm forced to, not because I'm afraid of losing you, and not because I'm waiting for something better. You don't have to compete with anyone, Hailey. There is no one you're competing with. I already chose you.", image: null }

,{ title: "My Apologies", message: "I have so many apologies for you and I owe you the love that you deserve. Hopefully soon mabigyan ng pagkakataon para iparamdam sa'yo lahat. I know I have not been the best guy na nakilala mo, and I know I have shortcomings that have hurt you in ways I probably didn't realize at first. I'm genuinely sorry for all of them. I'm sorry sa mga bagay na expected mo na dapat ginagawa ko to prove my love, pero hindi mo nakita from me. I'm sorry if there were moments na you needed me to show you that I love you, pero instead, I became quiet, cold, or distant. I'm sorry if sometimes I prefer keeping my feelings to myself instead of expressing them to you. I'm sorry if I ever made you feel like you weren't loved enough by me. I really, really hate knowing that I made you feel that way, especially when loving you was never supposed to make you feel unwanted or uncertain. I'm sorry if I did something that made you overthink, question my intentions, or even question whether I'm really the right guy for you. I'm sorry for every time I made you feel bad, every time I made you doubt yourself, and every time I made you feel like you are a terrible person. I'm sorry if I'm not verbally sweet or affectionate sa'yo. I'm sorry if I'm not always the guy who knows exactly what to say when you need reassurance or comforting words. I'm sorry if I'm not the guy who knows how to lead, take care of you, protect you, and make you feel na mahal na mahal ka. Sometimes puro salita lang ako, and I know words mean very little when my actions don't follow them. And sometimes, alam ko naman na I'm doing something na hindi mo gusto, yet I still can't help myself from doing it. Not because I don't care about you, but because there are parts of myself that are still hurting. And instead of facing that pain properly, I shut down. I become cold. I distance myself. And I know that isn't fair to you. You shouldn't have to always be the one leading the way. You shouldn't have to constantly teach me how to love you, remind me how to treat you, or carry the emotional weight of our relationship. You deserve to feel cared for without having to ask for every little thing. You deserve someone who doesn't make you feel like you have to fight just to feel loved And I'm sorry that there were times I became the reason you felt bad when I was supposed to be someone who made you feel safe, loved, and appreciated.I'm not saying all of this because I want you to immediately forgive me or forget everything that happened. I know an apology doesn't erase the things I did or the feelings I caused. And I don't want to promise you that I'll magically become a different person overnight. But I am trying. I'm trying to become a better version of myself, not just by saying that I will change, but by actually understanding the parts of myself that need to change. I'll use this time na friends muna tayo to work on myself, unlearn the things that hurt you, and learn how to love someone in a way that they can actually feel. Salamat sa'yo, kasi you became one of the biggest reasons kung bakit gusto kong baguhin yung mga nakagawian ko. You showed me that love isn't only about what I feel inside. It's also about how I make the person I love feel through my actions. You're one of the reasons why I want to become better. And if someday mabigyan man tayo ulit ng pagkakataon, I hope by then, I won't just tell you that I've changed. I hope you'll be able to feel it in the way I treat you, the way I communicate with you, the way I take care of you, and the way I love you. Sana kung mangyari man iyon, sa'yo ko pa rin maiparamdam lahat ng pagmamahal na natutunan kong ipakita nang tama. And this time, I don't want my shortcomings to be the reason that love between us gets held back again. I'm truly sorry, Hailey. For everything I did, everything I failed to do, and everything I made you feel. You deserved better from me, and I'm sorry that I had to hurt you before I fully understood that.", image: null }
  
  
  ,{ title: "I'm Yearning For Your Old Soul", message: "Sometimes, I wish I am the guy you're most comfortable with. When you have a problem, I'm the first one na lalapitan mo to talk, to vent your thoughts, the one who will comfort you. I wish that I'm the first guy that you'll find whether you are happy, sad, frustrated, or emotional. I wish na we were seeing each other like a best friend while in a low-key relationship, na even though may mga friends tayo, ang isa't isa pa rin ang hahanapin. To be honest, mas gugustuhin ko pa na ipakita mo ang weird side mo sa akin at maging comfortable kaysa i-filter out yung mga actions and words mo toward me, afraid na baka ma-turn off ako. Kaya nga ako na-fall sa'yo in the first place kasi comfortable ka pag kasama mo ako eh. Malaya ka sa kahit anong sabihin at gawin mo. You didn't have to think twice before teasing me, saying something random, being weird, or simply being yourself. Pero now, nagbago ka na. I understand that some unfortunate things happened to you, and I know that those experiences shaped you into the person you are now. Maybe they taught you to be more careful. Maybe they made you think twice before showing too much of yourself. Maybe you learned that being vulnerable can sometimes hurt. And I don't blame you for that. But I really, really miss that part of you.I miss the girl who didn't have to filter herself around me. I miss our playful teasing, our random banters, the little things we used to say to each other, and those moments when we could just be stupid together without caring how we looked. I miss how you could say whatever was on your mind without worrying about whether I'd judge you for it.Sometimes, I feel like you're trying too hard to be the version of yourself that you think I would like. You try to be more mature, more composed, more careful with your words and actions. And I understand why. Maybe you want to keep my approval. Maybe you're afraid that if I see too much of the real you, I'll eventually get tired or turned off. But the truth is, you don't have to win my approval by becoming someone else. I never fell for the perfectly composed version of you. I fell for the girl who was comfortable enough to be weird around me. The girl who teased me without thinking twice. The girl who could be playful, childish, annoying, sweet, and completely herself. I don't want you to feel like you have to be careful around me just because we're together. I don't want you constantly wondering whether what you're about to say is too much, too dark, too weird, or not mature enough. You don't have to impress me. You don't have to prove that you're mature enough for me. You don't have to carefully choose every word just to make sure I won't change the way I see you. If anything, I wish you'd let yourself breathe around me again. I want to know what you actually want to say, even if it's random. I want to hear your stupid jokes. I want to see your weird side. I want to tease you and be teased back. I want those little moments where neither of us has to think about how we're supposed to act. Because that's the version of you I miss. Not because I think the person you've become is worse. I just miss the version of you who felt completely safe with me. And maybe that's what hurts the most. I know you're still here. We still talk. We still have our moments. I know you love me, and I don't question that. But sometimes, I still find myself yearning for the old you, the girl who made me feel like I wasn't just someone she loved, but someone she could completely be herself with. I don't want to take away the person you've become. I don't want to force you to go back to who you were. I just want you to know that if that playful, weird, unfiltered girl is still somewhere inside you, she doesn't have to hide from me. She never had to. And if life has made you more guarded, I hope someday it also gives you enough good reasons to feel safe again. Especially with me. Because I really, really miss you. Not the person you used to be. But the part of you that used to feel free when you were with me.", image: null },
  
  
  
